    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "\"The RASS and PLUTO databases are collections of geochemical data maintained by the USGS, Branch of Geochemistry.  These data have been collected over a period of time extending from the present to as far back as the 1930's for the PLUTO data and the 1960's for the RASS data.  Scientific methods, instrumentation, and detection levels have changed significantly over this period of time.  Thus, researchers are likely to find data from more than one analytical method and reporting more than one lower determination limit for any given element.  All of the data are reported in parts per million unless designated as percent.\"",
